IMPORT prelude

-- Minors' Contracts Act 1987 (Singapore) -- the whole operative text: the Infants Relief Act 1874 disapplied (s 1), guarantees of a
-- minor's obligations (s 2), restitution of property a minor acquired under a contract (s 3), and the transitional rule for
-- contracts made between 9 April 1987 and 12 November 1993 (s 4).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation ("version in force from 1/4/2022"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/MCA1987.txt. The edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"; the
-- latest amendment annotated is Act 25 of 2021 (Courts (Civil and Criminal Justice) Reform Act 2021, s 163), in force 1 April 2022,
-- annotated against s 3(1) and (2). The deposit does not show what the amendment changed. The Legislative History says this is the
-- U.K. Minors' Contracts Act 1987 (c. 13), declared to apply in Singapore by the Application of English Law Act 1993 from
-- 12 November 1993.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for everyday-life relevance (Tier 1): it decides what happens when a shop, lender or landlord deals with
-- someone under age -- whether a parent who guaranteed the deal is still liable, and whether the goods can be got back. SCOPED to
-- the whole Act, which has four operative sections. Not encoded: who is a "minor" and when a minor's contract is unenforceable or
-- may be repudiated -- the Act does NOT say; that comes from the common law and other Acts (none was read). The content of s 5 of
-- the Civil Law Act 1909 as in force before 12 November 1993, on which s 4 turns, is not in the deposit and is taken as an input.
--
-- Dates are written as a number YYYYMMDD (9 April 1987 is 19870409) so that ordinary comparison gives date order.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Minors' Contracts Act 1987 -- contracts`

DECLARE Contract HAS
    `made on` IS A NUMBER
    `the Act applied to it under Civil Law Act s 5 before 12 November 1993` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is unenforceable against the minor or the minor repudiates it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that is because the party was a minor when it was made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a guarantee was given for the minor's obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the minor acquired property under it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the minor still holds that property or property representing it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court thinks it just and equitable` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `4 -- contracts before 12 November 1993`

-- s 4: "Nothing in this Act applies in relation to a contract made after 9 April 1987 and before 12 November 1993 except in so far
-- as it was applicable by virtue of section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 in force before 12 November 1993."
-- Long title date: [12 November 1993]. Every operative section speaks only of contracts made "after 9 April 1987", so a contract
-- made ON 9 April 1987 is outside all of them.
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act reaches the contract` IF
        `the contract`'s `made on` GREATER THAN 19870409
    AND (    `the contract`'s `made on` AT LEAST 19931112
         OR  `the contract`'s `the Act applied to it under Civil Law Act s 5 before 12 November 1993`)

§§ `1 -- Infants Relief Act 1874 disapplied`

-- s 1: "The Infants Relief Act 1874 (which invalidates certain contracts made by minors and prohibits actions to enforce contracts
-- ratified after majority) shall not apply to any contract made by a minor after 9 April 1987."
-- The rule says only that the 1874 Act is disapplied. Whether the 1874 Act otherwise applied in Singapore to an older contract is
-- not stated in the deposit, so this encodes "s 1 disapplies it", not "the 1874 Act applies".
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 1 disapplies the Infants Relief Act 1874` IF
    `the Act reaches the contract` `the contract`

§§ `2 -- guarantees`

-- s 2: where "(a) a guarantee is given in respect of an obligation of a party to a contract made after 9 April 1987; and (b) the
-- obligation is unenforceable against him (or he repudiates the contract) because he was a minor when the contract was made, the
-- guarantee shall not for that reason alone be unenforceable against the guarantor."
-- "For that reason alone": the guarantor loses only the minority defence. Any other defence to the guarantee is untouched, and the
-- section does not say the guarantee IS enforceable. The result here is therefore "minority is no defence for the guarantor".
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the guarantor cannot rely on the minority` IF
        `the Act reaches the contract` `the contract`
    AND `the contract`'s `a guarantee was given for the minor's obligation`
    AND `the contract`'s `it is unenforceable against the minor or the minor repudiates it`
    AND `the contract`'s `that is because the party was a minor when it was made`

§§ `3 -- restitution`

-- s 3(1): where "(a) a person (the claimant) has after 9 April 1987 entered into a contract with another (the defendant); and (b)
-- the contract is unenforceable against the defendant (or he repudiates it) because he was a minor when the contract was made, the
-- court MAY, if it is just and equitable to do so, require the defendant to transfer to the claimant any property acquired by the
-- defendant under the contract, or any property representing it." [Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022]
-- s 3(2): "Nothing in this section shall be taken to prejudice any other remedy available to the claimant."
-- The power is discretionary ("may") and limited to property: the section gives no money judgment for the price or for damages.
-- Whether the minor must still hold the property is not said in so many words; it is inferred from "transfer ... any property
-- acquired ... or any property representing it" -- a court cannot order the transfer of property the minor no longer has.
GIVEN `the contract` IS A Contract
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may order the minor to transfer the property` IF
        `the Act reaches the contract` `the contract`
    AND `the contract`'s `it is unenforceable against the minor or the minor repudiates it`
    AND `the contract`'s `that is because the party was a minor when it was made`
    AND `the contract`'s `the minor acquired property under it`
    AND `the contract`'s `the minor still holds that property or property representing it`
    AND `the contract`'s `the court thinks it just and equitable`

DECLARE Order IS ONE OF
    `return of the goods the minor acquired`
    `transfer of property representing the goods`
    `payment of the unpaid price`
    `damages for breach of the contract`

-- What an order under s 3(1) can be. That the proceeds of a resale count as "property representing it" is an inference from the
-- words, not stated.
GIVEN `the order` IS AN Order
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 3 can make the order` IF
    CONSIDER `the order`
    WHEN `return of the goods the minor acquired` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `transfer of property representing the goods` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
